# Work Methodology

## Branching Strategy

- `main` — stable, production-ready code only
- `develop` — integration branch; all PRs target `develop`, never `main`
- Feature branches: `feat/<short-description>` (e.g. `feat/hosts-rollback`)
- Bug fixes: `fix/<short-description>` (e.g. `fix/toggle-state-sync`)
- Chores: `chore/<short-description>` (e.g. `chore/update-deps`)
- CI triggers releases from merges into `develop` → `main`

## Versioning

Format: `YY.M.PATCH` (e.g. `26.5.3` = June 2026, patch 3).

Version must be kept in sync across **4 files** — always update all of them together:
- `VERSION`
- `package.json`
- `src-tauri/Cargo.toml`
- `src-tauri/tauri.conf.json`

Use the CI script `scripts/ci-tag-version-push.sh` to bump; avoid manual edits.

## Commit Messages

Follow Conventional Commits:
```
feat: add hosts rollback on auth failure
fix: sync editor state when context reloads
chore: bump dependencies
docs: update README CI workflow name
```

## Code Review Checklist

Before opening a PR, verify:
- [ ] No `unwrap()` added in Rust without justification
- [ ] Errors surfaced to the user (toast/dialog), not swallowed
- [ ] Dead code removed, not commented out
- [ ] Hosts apply is transactional (apply before persist, or revert on failure)
- [ ] README and docs reflect the actual behavior

## Testing

- Unit tests live in `src-tauri/src/` using `#[cfg(test)]` modules
- Frontend integration tests are not yet set up — add them before shipping new critical paths
- Always add a test for `hosts.rs` logic when modifying `build_managed_block` or `strip_managed_section`
